<title>JAPAN: Shizuoka Bank to change rules for share buyback.</title>
<headline>Shizuoka Bank to change rules for share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shizuoka Bank Ltd said on Tuesday it plans to change its company regulations at a shareholders' meeting scheduled for June 27 to allow it to buy back its shares.  </p>
<p>&quot;It's part of our capital management policy to have the option of buying back the company's shares if it is deemed desirable,&quot; a bank spokesman said.</p>
<p>He said the rule change would allow the bank to repurchase up to 80 million of its shares.</p>
</text>
